## Claude Code specifics

- Skills: `{{claude_skills_dir}}/` holds the Lumina skills ({{skill_names}}); Claude Code loads them by their
  descriptions. Use `lumina-mcp` to connect to the running editor and `lumina-engine` before working in a new area.
- Connect to the editor's MCP server with the command Tools → AI Agent Access (MCP) shows
  (`claude mcp add --transport http lumina <url> --header "Authorization: Bearer <token>"`); the token changes
  each editor session, so re-add it after the editor restarts.
- Put rules every agent should follow in `AGENTS.md`, and Claude-only notes here.
